  "question": {
    "html": "<p>Element <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"_{13}^{26}\\textrm{X}\"></span> decays into element Y through 4<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\alpha\"></span> and 2<span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\beta^{-}\"></span> emissions. The average binding energy per nucleon of element X is twice that of Y. The total energy needed to separate the nucleons of one <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"_{13}^{26}\\textrm{X}\"></span> nucleus is 130 MeV.</p>\n<p>What is the total energy needed to separate the nucleons of one nucleus of Y?</p>\n<p></p>\n<ol class=\"mcq-options\">\n<li data-label=\"A\">25 MeV</li>\n<li data-label=\"B\">45 MeV</li>\n<li data-label=\"C\">50 MeV</li>\n<li data-label=\"D\">90 MeV</li>\n</ol>"
